  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study is a theoretical and conceptual analysis of a document type rather than an empirical evaluation of specific collision datasets or driver behaviors.",
      "what": "This study analyzes the European Accident Statement (EAS) to demonstrate how standardized collision forms translate physical and emotional traffic violence into structured, administratively manageable events. Drawing on ethnomethodology, phenomenology, and science and technology studies, the paper conceptualizes these documents as 'text acts' that actively reconstruct the social and epistemic order of mobility.",
      "why": "It reveals that the continuity of automobility relies on mundane bureaucratic paperwork to frame systemic traffic violence as isolated, episodic occurrences, thereby restoring traffic flow and normalizing vehicular harm."
    }
